{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Who makes</b> — the sense is that HaShem can do all He desires, for He makes heaven and earth, the sea, and all that is in them. <b>Heaven</b> — these are the angels and the great host, they are the ministers; and on earth, the bird and the beast and man; and in the sea, great creatures." "<b>Who keeps truth forever</b> — these are the generalities of every species that are on earth and in the sea; only in heaven, all that are in them in their particulars are kept forever. Therefore do not fear man, who would oppress you, and He gives your bread, and He releases your bonds."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 146, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:57.451770580Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}